      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense, but \"future-proofing\" might feel a bit vague to their CTO. He's pretty data-driven and usually pushes back if he thinks we're just selling him something \"just in case.\"\n\nIs there any way we can point to specific, even if hypothetical, risks or vulnerabilities that the current audit *didn't* catch? Like, can we suggest that their current stability might actually be masking some deeper, more sophisticated patterns that only the premium package would flag? I need something a bit more concrete to justify the extra spend.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
